# complexity.allow — cyclomatic-complexity allow-list for scripts/check-complexity.py
#
# This file captures the functions the LIVE graph reports over complexity 60
# (see scripts/check-complexity.py --report), so the complexity gate lands
# green against the tree as it exists today. Generated code is excluded from
# the population outright (tools/tree-sitter parsers, generated/ trees) — a
# gate counting those measures a code generator, not this codebase.
#
# The list is an EXACT snapshot, not a ceiling. The gate fails both ways: a
# function over threshold with no line here is a new violation, and a line
# here whose function is gone or back under threshold is a permission that
# outlived the debt it excused. So once a function is brought back under 60,
# deleting its line is mandatory — and that deletion is what makes crossing
# 60 again forbidden from then on.
#
# Format: <file_path>:<function_name>  # <complexity at time of entry>
# file_path is project-relative; function_name is the bare symbol (the
# qualified_name's project/module prefix is machine-specific and does not
# belong in a committed allow-list).
#
# Regenerate the body (never hand-edit the entry list) with:
#     scripts/check-complexity.py --report

